WEBVTT

00:08:27.961 --> 00:08:31.469
and he said, "I've got
the perfect place for you."

00:08:31.493 --> 00:08:33.477
"Really?" I said. I'm
always a bit skeptical

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:34.955
when people say things like that.

00:08:34.979 --> 00:08:36.325
"No, honestly," he went on,

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:38.171
"it's only three hours away by car,

00:08:38.195 --> 00:08:39.785
and it's not very expensive,

00:08:39.809 --> 00:08:43.365
and it's probably not like anywhere
you've stayed before."

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:47.564
"Hmm." I was beginning to get
slightly intrigued. "What is it?"

00:08:47.588 --> 00:08:50.343
"Well —" Here my friend hemmed and hawed —

00:08:50.367 --> 00:08:53.925
"Well, actually
it's a Catholic hermitage."

00:08:53.949 --> 00:08:55.891
This was the wrong answer.

00:08:55.915 --> 00:08:58.438
I had spent 15 years in Anglican schools,

00:08:58.462 --> 00:09:03.036
so I had had enough hymnals
and crosses to last me a lifetime.